The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!info->fbcon_par)
    con2fb_acquire_newinfo(vc, info, vc->vc_num);
par = info->fbcon_par;
par->cur_blink_jiffies = msecs_to_jiffies(vc->vc_cur_blink_ms);
Reason:
The return value of `con2fb_acquire_newinfo()` is not checked. If it fails (e.g., due to `fbcon_open()` failure), `info->fbcon_par` remains NULL. The subsequent code dereferences `info->fbcon_par` (via `par`) without validation, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!info->fbcon_par)
    if (con2fb_acquire_newinfo(vc, info, vc->vc_num))
        return;
Reason:
By checking the return value of `con2fb_acquire_newinfo()`, the function returns early on failure, preventing any further operations on `info->fbcon_par` when it is still NULL. This avoids the null pointer dereference.

